<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49505" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turrĭger</span></b> , gĕra.
		gĕrum. adj.
		turris-gero, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>turret-bearing</i>, <i>turreted.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen. (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">umeri elephantorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 2, 1, § 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ferae moles,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
				9</span></i>
			,  560: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 10, 253</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ripae, Claud. Cons. Prob. et Olybr. 229:
					Antemnae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 7, 631</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					3, 514</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4,
			226</span></i>.—Of a city: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patriae imago turrigero canos effundens vertice
					crines,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					1, 188</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tur-rĭgĕra</span></b> , ae, <i>adj. f.</i>, <i>turret - crowned</i>,
				<i>turreled</i>, an epithet of Cybele, who was
			represented with a crown of turrets (personifying the earth and its
			cities): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cybele,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					6, 321</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 4, 224</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ops,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Tr.
					2, 24</span></i>
			.</div>
